00:45:57,800 --> 00:46:00,950
Then it saw all people as a threat.
Not just the ones on the other side.

241
00:46:02,960 --> 00:46:05,750
It decided our fate in a microsecond.

242
00:46:07,440 --> 00:46:09,190
Extermination.

243
00:46:23,560 --> 00:46:25,070
Did you see this war?

244
00:46:37,520 --> 00:46:42,270
No. I grew up after. In the ruins.

245
00:46:42,480 --> 00:46:45,510
Starving. Hiding from the H-Ks.

246
00:46:45,680 --> 00:46:48,670
- H-Ks?
- Hunter-killers.

247
00:46:48,840 --> 00:46:52,590
Patrol machines
built in automated factories.

248
00:46:52,760 --> 00:46:57,030
Most of us were rounded up,
put in camps for orderly disposal.

249
00:46:59,080 --> 00:47:01,350
This was burned in by laser scanner.

250
00:47:05,320 --> 00:47:09,870
Some of us were kept alive. To work.

251
00:47:10,840 --> 00:47:12,190
Loading bodies.

252
00:47:13,320 --> 00:47:16,030
The disposal units ran night and day.

253
00:47:16,200 --> 00:47:19,070
We were that close
to going out forever.

254
00:47:22,160 --> 00:47:26,030
But there was one man
who taught us to fight.

255
00:47:26,200 --> 00:47:28,110
To storm the wire of the camps.

256
00:47:28,320 --> 00:47:31,590
To smash those metal
motherfuckers into junk.

257
00:47:33,240 --> 00:47:35,950
He turned it around.
He brought us back from the brink.

258
00:47:36,160 --> 00:47:40,390
His name was Connor. John Connor.

259
00:47:40,560 --> 00:47:45,030
Your son, Sarah. Your unborn son.

260
00:49:34,800 --> 00:49:35,790
Drive!

261
00:49:43,120 --> 00:49:46,190
Reese!

262
00:50:04,200 --> 00:50:07,590
No, Reese. No, no, no. They'll kill you.

263
00:50:07,760 --> 00:50:10,590
You in the Cadillac,
let me see your hands now.

264
00:50:13,760 --> 00:50:14,750
Get out of the car.

265
00:50:18,520 --> 00:50:20,710
Drop to your knees.

266
00:50:20,880 --> 00:50:23,510
- Out of the car.
- Drop to the ground.

267
00:50:52,840 --> 00:50:56,750
Sarah. Sarah, try to drink some of this.

268
00:50:59,760 --> 00:51:01,910
Listen, are you sure it's them?

269
00:51:02,120 --> 00:51:04,870
I mean,
maybe I should look at the bodies.

270
00:51:05,080 --> 00:51:07,910
No. They've been identified
and there's no doubt.

271
00:51:11,760 --> 00:51:13,630
Ginger.

272
00:51:15,240 --> 00:51:18,710
- Kiddo.
- Sarah...

273
00:51:18,880 --> 00:51:22,030
- Sarah, this is Dr. Silberman.
- Hi, Sarah.

274
00:51:22,200 --> 00:51:26,230
I want you to tell him everything
Reese told you. Do you feel up to that?

275
00:51:26,400 --> 00:51:28,510
Yeah, I guess so.

276
00:51:30,280 --> 00:51:34,110
- You're a doctor?
- Criminal psychologist.

277
00:51:34,280 --> 00:51:38,510
- Is Reese crazy?
- That's what we're gonna find out.

278
00:53:03,720 --> 00:53:07,230
So you're a soldier. Fighting for whom?

279
00:53:08,720 --> 00:53:13,750
With the 132nd under Perry.
From '21 to '27.

280
00:53:14,560 --> 00:53:17,030
That's the year 2027?

281
00:53:17,200 --> 00:53:19,270
That's right. Then I was assigned...

282
00:53:19,440 --> 00:53:23,070
- This is fucking great.
-... under John Connor.

283
00:53:23,240 --> 00:53:26,310
- Who was the enemy?
- A computer defense system built...

284
00:53:26,480 --> 00:53:29,030
Goddamn. Sorry.

285
00:53:29,200 --> 00:53:32,550
... built for SAC-NORAD
by Cyberdyne Systems.

286
00:53:32,720 --> 00:53:34,670
I see.

287
00:53:34,840 --> 00:53:40,710
And this computer thinks it can win
by killing the mother of its enemy.

288
00:53:40,880 --> 00:53:44,070
Killing him, in effect,
before he's even conceived.

289
00:53:44,280 --> 00:53:46,350
A sort of retroactive abortion?

290
00:53:48,160 --> 00:53:51,390
Silberman cracks me up.
Last week, a guy burned his Afghan.

291
00:53:51,560 --> 00:53:54,070
- He screwed it first...
- Ed, shut up.

292
00:53:54,240 --> 00:53:56,550
Why didn't the computer
just kill Connor then?

293
00:53:56,720 --> 00:53:59,270
Why this elaborate scheme
with the Terminator?

294
00:53:59,440 --> 00:54:03,510
It had no choice.
Their defense grid was smashed.

295
00:54:03,680 --> 00:54:08,110
We'd won. Taking out Connor then
would make no difference.

296
00:54:08,280 --> 00:54:11,070
Skynet had to wipe out
his entire existence.

297
00:54:11,240 --> 00:54:16,270
Is that when you captured the lab
complex and found... What is it called?

298
00:54:16,480 --> 00:54:18,630
The time displacement equipment?

299
00:54:18,800 --> 00:54:22,830
That's right. The Terminator
had already gone through.

300
00:54:23,000 --> 00:54:25,870
Connor sent me to intercept
and they blew the whole place.

301
00:54:26,040 --> 00:54:27,870
Well, how are you supposed to get back?

302
00:54:28,760 --> 00:54:30,470
I can't.

303
00:54:31,960 --> 00:54:37,550
Nobody goes home.
Nobody else comes through.

304
00:54:38,320 --> 00:54:41,390
It's just him and me.

305
00:56:25,840 --> 00:56:28,670
It's just him and me.

306
00:56:31,760 --> 00:56:36,710
Why didn't you bring any weapons?
Something more advanced.

307
00:56:36,880 --> 00:56:39,830
Don't you have ray guns?

308
00:56:40,040 --> 00:56:43,670
- Ray guns.
- Show me a piece of future technology.

309
00:56:43,840 --> 00:56:48,230
You go naked. Something about the
field generated by a living organism.

310
00:56:48,400 --> 00:56:50,430
- Nothing dead will go.
- Why?

311
00:56:50,600 --> 00:56:52,270
I didn't build the fucking thing.

312
00:56:52,440 --> 00:56:57,190
OK, OK. But this cyborg,
if it's metal... ?

313
00:56:57,360 --> 00:56:59,790
- Surrounded by living tissue.
- Oh, right.

314
00:57:00,600 --> 00:57:03,310
This is great stuff.
I could make a career out of this guy.

315
00:57:03,520 --> 00:57:06,270
See how clever it is?
It doesn't require a shred of proof.

316
00:57:06,480 --> 00:57:09,910
Most paranoid delusions are intricate,
but this is brilliant.

317
00:57:12,280 --> 00:57:14,270
- Why were the other
two women killed?

318
00:57:14,270 --> 00:57:16,230
- Most records were
lost in the war.

319
00:57:16,400 --> 00:57:18,950
Skynet knew almost nothing
about Connor's mother.

320
00:57:19,160 --> 00:57:22,550
Her full name, where she lived.
They just knew the city.

321
00:57:22,720 --> 00:57:25,790
The Terminator was
just being systematic.

322
00:57:26,000 --> 00:57:28,830
- Let's go back...
- Look, you have heard enough.

323
00:57:29,000 --> 00:57:31,950
I have answered your questions,
now I have to see Sarah Connor.

324
00:57:32,120 --> 00:57:35,970
- I'm afraid that's not up to me.
- Then why am I talking to you?

325
00:57:36,040 --> 00:57:38,070
- Who is in authority here?
- Please...

326
00:57:38,240 --> 00:57:39,790
Shut up!

327
00:57:40,560 --> 00:57:43,150
You still don't get it, do you?

328
00:57:43,320 --> 00:57:48,430
He'll find her. That's what he does.
That's all he does.

329
00:57:48,600 --> 00:57:50,350
You can't stop him.

330
00:57:50,520 --> 00:57:54,110
He'll reach down her throat
and pull her fucking heart out!

331
00:57:54,320 --> 00:57:57,270
- Doc.
- Let go of me!

332
00:58:00,720 --> 00:58:01,710
Sorry.

333
00:58:07,160 --> 00:58:08,510
So Reese is crazy?

334
00:58:08,680 --> 00:58:12,190
In technical terminology, he's a loon.

335
00:58:13,040 --> 00:58:18,470
Sarah, this is what they call
body armor. Our TAC guys wear these.

336
00:58:18,680 --> 00:58:20,690
It'll stop a 12-gauge round.

337
00:58:20,760 --> 00:58:23,250
This other individual must've
been wearing one under his coat.

338
00:58:23,320 --> 00:58:24,990
Feel that. Go ahead.

339
00:58:27,280 --> 00:58:30,870
- He punched through the windshield.
- He was probably on PCP.

340
00:58:31,040 --> 00:58:33,710
Broke every bone in his hand.
He wouldn't feel it for hours.

341
00:58:33,780 --> 00:58:35,570
There was this guy once...
You see this scar?

342
00:58:35,640 --> 00:58:37,030
- Here.
- Thank you.

343
00:58:38,480 --> 00:58:42,230
There's a couch in this other room.
Stretch out and get some sleep.

344
00:58:42,300 --> 00:58:44,810
Be at least an hour before
your mother gets here from Big Bear.

345
00:58:44,880 --> 00:58:47,990
- I can't sleep.
- Try.

346
00:58:48,160 --> 00:58:52,390
It may not look it,
but that couch is very comfortable.

347
00:58:53,680 --> 00:58:58,190
You'll be perfectly safe.
We got 30 cops in this building.

348
00:58:59,080 --> 00:59:00,310
Thank you.

349
00:59:06,800 --> 00:59:08,630
- Good night.
- Good night.

350
00:59:23,480 --> 00:59:27,110
I'm a friend of Sarah Connor.
I was told she's here. Could I see her?

351
00:59:27,280 --> 00:59:29,430
No. Can't see her.
She's making a statement.

352
00:59:29,600 --> 00:59:30,710
Where is she?

353
00:59:31,680 --> 00:59:34,470
It may take a while. If you wanna wait,
there's a bench over there.

354
00:59:46,040 --> 00:59:47,550
I'll be back.

355
01:00:36,000 --> 01:00:38,550
- Are they terrorists?
- Let's go, let's go!

356
01:00:43,240 --> 01:00:44,590
Stay here.

357
01:00:58,840 --> 01:01:00,350
Let's get outta here!

358
01:01:24,800 --> 01:01:25,910
Watch him.

359
01:02:33,800 --> 01:02:35,110
Ed...

360
01:02:36,000 --> 01:02:37,310
Hey!

361
01:03:04,040 --> 01:03:05,470
Sarah!

362
01:03:06,840 --> 01:03:08,150
Reese.

363
01:03:12,080 --> 01:03:13,230
This way.

364
01:03:54,040 --> 01:03:56,710
KFLB news time 4:36.

365
01:03:56,880 --> 01:04:00,590
Top story of the hour: the largest
single law enforcement mobilization

366
01:04:00,760 --> 01:04:03,310
in California history
is currently underway.

367
01:04:03,520 --> 01:04:07,070
Police in five counties are engaged
in a massive manhunt for...

368
01:04:10,680 --> 01:04:12,030
Take this.

369
01:04:15,160 --> 01:04:16,830
All right,
let's get this off the road.

370
01:04:48,840 --> 01:04:51,710
- You cold?
- Freezing.

371
01:05:05,680 --> 01:05:06,870
Reese?

372
01:05:08,760 --> 01:05:12,470
- You got a first name?
- Kyle.

373
01:05:12,640 --> 01:05:16,950
Kyle, what's it like
when you go through time?

374
01:05:19,800 --> 01:05:21,630
White light.

375
01:05:24,080 --> 01:05:25,430
Pain.

376
01:05:28,720 --> 01:05:32,950
- It's like being born maybe.
- Oh, my God.

377
01:05:33,880 --> 01:05:35,790
I caught one back there.

378
01:05:37,400 --> 01:05:40,150
- You mean you got shot?
- It's not bad.

379
01:05:41,040 --> 01:05:44,470
- We gotta get you to a doctor.
- It's OK. Forget it.

380
01:05:44,640 --> 01:05:49,310
What do you mean, forget it?
Are you crazy? Take this off.

381
01:06:01,600 --> 01:06:03,590
Jesus.

382
01:06:03,760 --> 01:06:06,630
See? It passed right through the meat.

383
01:06:06,800 --> 01:06:08,430
This is gonna make me puke.

384
01:06:09,160 --> 01:06:11,950
- Would you just talk about something?
- What?

385
01:06:12,120 --> 01:06:15,590
I don't know. Anything.
Just talk. Tell me about my son.

386
01:06:17,440 --> 01:06:18,990
He's about my height.

387
01:06:22,680 --> 01:06:24,670
He has your eyes.

388
01:06:28,040 --> 01:06:29,590
What's he like?

389
01:06:30,400 --> 01:06:34,070
You trust him. He's got a strength.

390
01:06:35,800 --> 01:06:37,630
I'd die for John Connor.

391
01:06:40,560 --> 01:06:44,190
Well, at least now I know
what to name him.

392
01:06:45,360 --> 01:06:50,110
Don't suppose you know who the father is
so I won't tell him to get lost?

393
01:06:50,280 --> 01:06:53,030
John never said much about him.

394
01:06:53,200 --> 01:06:55,710
- I know he dies before the war...
- Wait.

395
01:06:57,640 --> 01:06:59,430
I don't wanna know.

396
01:07:00,720 --> 01:07:03,430
So was it John that sent you here?

397
01:07:04,160 --> 01:07:05,670
I volunteered.

398
01:07:06,920 --> 01:07:10,710
- Why?
- It was a chance to meet the legend.

399
01:07:11,800 --> 01:07:18,630
Sarah Connor,
who taught her son to fight, organize,

400
01:07:18,840 --> 01:07:20,910
prepare from when he was a kid.

401
01:07:21,080 --> 01:07:23,110
When you were in hiding before the war.

402
01:07:27,240 --> 01:07:30,670
You're talking about things
I haven't done yet in the past tense.

403
01:07:30,840 --> 01:07:32,710
It's driving me crazy.

404
01:07:36,600 --> 01:07:39,350
Are you sure you have the right person?

405
01:07:39,520 --> 01:07:41,550
I'm sure.

406
01:07:41,720 --> 01:07:45,430
Come on. Do I look like
the mother of the future?

407
01:07:47,280 --> 01:07:52,110
I mean, am I tough? Organized?
I can't even balance my checkbook.

408
01:07:54,920 --> 01:07:59,030
Look, Reese, I didn't ask
for this honor and I don't want it.

409
01:07:59,200 --> 01:08:00,630
Any of it.

410
01:08:03,960 --> 01:08:08,150
Your son gave me a message
to give to you. Made me memorize it.

411
01:08:09,520 --> 01:08:12,190
"Thank you, Sarah,
for your courage through the dark years.

412
01:08:12,360 --> 01:08:14,510
I can't help you with
what you must soon face,

413
01:08:14,680 --> 01:08:16,950
except to say the future is not set.

414
01:08:17,120 --> 01:08:19,630
You must be stronger than
you imagine you can be.

415
01:08:19,800 --> 01:08:22,310
You must survive or I will never exist. "

416
01:08:23,640 --> 01:08:25,110
That's all.

417
01:08:28,080 --> 01:08:29,590
It's a good field dressing.

418
01:08:31,160 --> 01:08:32,630
You like it?

419
01:08:33,400 --> 01:08:34,790
It's my first.

420
01:08:39,120 --> 01:08:41,470
Get some sleep. It'll be light soon.

421
01:08:45,760 --> 01:08:46,990
OK.

422
01:08:57,680 --> 01:08:59,590
Talk to me some more.

423
01:09:02,840 --> 01:09:04,390
About what?

424
01:09:05,600 --> 01:09:07,710
Tell me about where you're from.

425
01:09:10,200 --> 01:09:11,670
All right.

426
01:09:13,600 --> 01:09:18,110
You stay down by day,
but at night you can move around.

427
01:09:18,280 --> 01:09:22,190
You still have to be careful
because the H-Ks use infrared.

428
01:09:24,320 --> 01:09:29,350
But they're not too bright.
John taught us ways to dust them.

429
01:09:30,840 --> 01:09:33,070
That's when the infiltrators
started to appear.

430
01:09:33,240 --> 01:09:35,270
The Terminators were the newest.

431
01:09:35,920 --> 01:09:36,830
The worst.

432
01:09:46,880 --> 01:09:49,280
Traversing your sector
in search mode.

433
01:09:49,280 --> 01:09:51,470
750 meters north of your position.

434
01:09:56,440 --> 01:09:57,550
Let's go.

435
01:10:43,040 --> 01:10:46,990
- Reese. DN384...
- Right. Let him in.

436
01:12:18,520 --> 01:12:20,350
Terminator!

437
01:13:37,640 --> 01:13:39,950
I was dreaming about dogs.

438
01:13:41,200 --> 01:13:43,590
We use 'em to spot Terminators.

439
01:13:44,680 --> 01:13:47,190
Your world is pretty terrifying.

440
01:14:26,000 --> 01:14:29,910
Hey, buddy,
you got a dead cat in there or what?

441
01:14:37,280 --> 01:14:39,430
Fuck you, asshole.

442
01:14:58,280 --> 01:15:00,110
God damn.

443
01:15:01,200 --> 01:15:02,670
Thank you.

444
01:15:08,040 --> 01:15:09,550
Is this enough?

445
01:15:10,200 --> 01:15:13,390
Yeah, it's enough.
I don't wanna ask where you got it.

446
01:15:19,720 --> 01:15:21,230
- I'm coming.
- We need a room.

447
01:15:21,400 --> 01:15:23,390
- All right.
- With a kitchen.

448
01:15:23,560 --> 01:15:25,030
Do you have one with a kitchen?

449
01:15:41,080 --> 01:15:43,910
I am dying for a shower.

450
01:15:45,560 --> 01:15:47,710
We should check your bandage, too.

451
01:15:48,280 --> 01:15:50,950
Later. I'm going out for supplies.

452
01:15:55,680 --> 01:15:56,830
Keep this.

453
01:16:22,920 --> 01:16:26,270
No, I can't tell you where I am, Mom.
I was told not to say.

454
01:16:26,440 --> 01:16:28,630
But I need to know where to reach you.

455
01:16:28,800 --> 01:16:33,910
You tell me to hide out at the cabin
and you won't tell me what's going on?

456
01:16:34,080 --> 01:16:36,830
I am worried sick here.

457
01:16:37,000 --> 01:16:40,750
OK. OK, here's the number.

458
01:16:40,920 --> 01:16:43,110
- You ready?
- Yes. Go ahead.

459
01:16:43,320 --> 01:16:49,990
It's 408-555-1439. Room nine.

460
01:16:50,160 --> 01:16:51,870
- Got it?
- I've got it.

461
01:16:52,080 --> 01:16:56,230
I gotta go. I'm sorry
I can't tell you more right now.

462
01:16:56,400 --> 01:16:58,150
I love you, Mom.

463
01:17:01,640 --> 01:17:03,510
I love you, too, sweetheart.

464
01:17:16,440 --> 01:17:18,830
- Tiki Motel.
- Give me your address there.

465
01:17:22,520 --> 01:17:23,590
What have we got?

466
01:17:27,320 --> 01:17:33,430
Mothballs... corn syrup... ammonia.

467
01:17:33,600 --> 01:17:35,230
What's for dinner?

468
01:17:35,960 --> 01:17:39,030
- Plastique.
- That sounds good.

469
01:17:39,200 --> 01:17:40,550
What is it?

470
01:17:41,480 --> 01:17:45,030
It's a nitroglycerin base.
It's a bit more stable.

471
01:17:45,200 --> 01:17:47,070
I learned to make it when I was a kid.

472
01:17:58,960 --> 01:18:01,070
Make sure there's none on the threads.

473
01:18:03,320 --> 01:18:04,710
Like this.

474
01:18:06,680 --> 01:18:08,470
Screw the end cap on.

475
01:18:10,400 --> 01:18:11,910
Very gently.

476
01:18:14,680 --> 01:18:16,990
You must've had a fun childhood.

477
01:18:20,680 --> 01:18:22,070
That's good.

478
01:18:23,040 --> 01:18:26,070
All right. Six more like that
and I'll get started on the fuses.

479
01:18:37,560 --> 01:18:39,510
He'll find us, won't he?

480
01:18:42,520 --> 01:18:43,990
Probably.

481
01:19:02,120 --> 01:19:04,230
It'll never be over, will it?

482
01:19:12,680 --> 01:19:14,670
Look at me. I'm shaking.

483
01:19:15,880 --> 01:19:20,950
Some legend.
You must be pretty disappointed.

484
01:19:22,040 --> 01:19:25,950
No, I'm not.

485
01:19:34,680 --> 01:19:39,990
Kyle, the women in your time,

486
01:19:40,160 --> 01:19:42,230
what are they like?

487
01:19:44,320 --> 01:19:46,390
Good fighters.

488
01:19:46,560 --> 01:19:48,590
That's not what I meant.

489
01:19:50,800 --> 01:19:52,630
Was there someone special?

490
01:19:54,680 --> 01:19:56,190
Someone... ?

491
01:19:56,840 --> 01:19:58,990
A girl, you know.

492
01:20:00,520 --> 01:20:01,870
No.

493
01:20:04,680 --> 01:20:06,310
Never.

494
01:20:07,880 --> 01:20:09,510
Never?

495
01:20:14,480 --> 01:20:17,830
I'm sorry. I'm so sorry.

496
01:20:20,720 --> 01:20:22,790
So much pain.

497
01:20:24,200 --> 01:20:28,510
Pain can be controlled.
You just disconnect it.

498
01:20:28,680 --> 01:20:30,950
So you feel nothing?

499
01:20:36,120 --> 01:20:39,030
John Connor gave me
a picture of you once.

500
01:20:40,960 --> 01:20:42,750
I didn't know why at the time.

501
01:20:44,200 --> 01:20:50,030
It was very old, torn, faded.

502
01:20:53,880 --> 01:20:59,870
You were young like you are now.
You seemed just a little sad.

503
01:21:01,440 --> 01:21:04,190
I used to always wonder
what you were thinking at that moment.

504
01:21:05,640 --> 01:21:07,870
I memorized every line...

505
01:21:09,360 --> 01:21:11,230
... every curve.

506
01:21:14,920 --> 01:21:16,830
I came across time for you, Sarah.

507
01:21:18,760 --> 01:21:23,030
I love you. I always have.

508
01:21:41,120 --> 01:21:42,750
I shouldn't have said that.

509
01:23:13,640 --> 01:23:14,870
Think fast.

510
01:24:44,920 --> 01:24:46,230
Trade places.

511
01:24:57,240 --> 01:25:00,590
Faster! Drive faster!

512
01:25:50,520 --> 01:25:53,670
Kyle! Oh, my God.

513
01:26:27,920 --> 01:26:29,270
Kyle.

514
01:26:44,520 --> 01:26:45,910
Son-of-a-bitch!

515
01:27:01,600 --> 01:27:02,590
You stay here.

516
01:27:26,560 --> 01:27:27,750
Let's get outta here.

517
01:27:31,400 --> 01:27:32,670
Get out.

518
01:27:49,800 --> 01:27:52,750
Kyle. Come on. Get up.

519
01:28:01,320 --> 01:28:03,870
Kyle, come on.

520
01:28:05,000 --> 01:28:07,870
Help me! Get out. Get out.

521
01:28:32,360 --> 01:28:34,310
Don't stop. Run!

522
01:30:46,480 --> 01:30:48,030
Sarah!

523
01:30:49,080 --> 01:30:50,670
Kyle.

524
01:30:56,000 --> 01:30:58,510
Kyle. Kyle...

525
01:31:00,640 --> 01:31:03,350
We did it, Kyle. We got him.

526
01:31:23,120 --> 01:31:26,030
No!

527
01:32:21,920 --> 01:32:23,190
Wait.

528
01:32:28,040 --> 01:32:29,670
What are you doing?

529
01:32:30,560 --> 01:32:33,710
Cover, so he can't track us.

530
01:32:43,440 --> 01:32:46,590
Come on! Come on.

531
01:32:46,760 --> 01:32:50,430
No, Kyle! Come on!

532
01:32:51,200 --> 01:32:52,950
- Come on!
- Leave me here.

533
01:33:04,080 --> 01:33:08,430
Move it, Reese! On your feet, soldier!

534
01:33:08,800 --> 01:33:10,950
On your feet!

535
01:33:11,600 --> 01:33:12,750
Move it!

536
01:34:24,440 --> 01:34:26,110
Get back. Go back.

537
01:35:00,640 --> 01:35:02,430
- Run, Sarah.
- No.

538
01:35:02,600 --> 01:35:09,310
Run!

539
01:35:09,920 --> 01:35:11,430
Come on, motherfucker.

540
01:37:04,440 --> 01:37:06,590
No.

541
01:39:05,120 --> 01:39:06,750
You're terminated, fucker.

542
01:40:04,960 --> 01:40:06,190
Kyle.

543
01:40:27,240 --> 01:40:31,230
Tape seven. November 10. Where was I?

544
01:40:32,200 --> 01:40:36,030
What's most difficult is trying to
decide what to tell you and what not to.

545
01:40:36,720 --> 01:40:40,750
But I guess I have a while before you're
old enough to understand these tapes.

546
01:40:40,920 --> 01:40:44,670
They're more for me at this point
just so that I can get it straight.

547
01:41:21,800 --> 01:41:23,110
Fill her up.

548
01:41:26,800 --> 01:41:29,910
Should I tell you about your father?

549
01:41:30,080 --> 01:41:32,310
Boy, that's a tough one.

550
01:41:33,880 --> 01:41:38,390
Will it affect your decision to send him
here, knowing that he is your father?

551
01:41:40,640 --> 01:41:43,390
If you don't send Kyle,
you can never be.

552
01:41:43,560 --> 01:41:46,630
God, a person could go crazy
thinking about this.

553
01:41:50,320 --> 01:41:52,190
I suppose I will tell you.

554
01:41:54,040 --> 01:41:55,790
I owe him that.

555
01:41:58,240 --> 01:42:00,550
Maybe it'll help if...

556
01:42:00,720 --> 01:42:06,150
... you know that in the few hours
that we had together...

557
01:42:07,840 --> 01:42:10,230
... we loved a lifetime's worth.

558
01:42:23,120 --> 01:42:26,950
- What did he just say?
- He says you're very beautiful.

559
01:42:27,160 --> 01:42:29,990
He is ashamed to ask you for five
American dollars for this picture.

560
01:42:30,200 --> 01:42:33,590
But if he doesn't,
his father will beat him.

561
01:42:33,760 --> 01:42:35,470
Pretty good hustle, kid.

562
01:42:52,840 --> 01:42:54,390
What did he just say?

563
01:42:55,160 --> 01:42:57,230
He said there's a storm coming in.

564
01:43:01,680 --> 01:43:03,270
I know.

565
01:43:34,000 --> 01:43:40,000
SubRip by

566
01:43:34,000 --> 01:43:40,000
HighCode

